hit@5 decreases, (4) no kind-FIGURE question in the top 5 under 295 (22 questions) leaves the top 5; among qualifying rows the highest MRR, then fewer candidates.
  296: FAILS (1) 32/42 < 33/42; (2) 20/30 < 21/30; (3) NVDA 8/14 < 9/14 (AAPL 13/14, MSFT 11/14 equal); (4) msft-04 4->8, nvda-01 3->8
  297: FAILS (1) passes 33/42; (2) passes 21/30; (3) NVDA 8/14 < 9/14 (AAPL 13/14 equal, MSFT 12/14 up); (4) msft-04 4->miss, nvda-01 3->miss
  298: FAILS (1) passes 34/42; (2) passes 22/30; (3) NVDA 8/14 < 9/14 (AAPL 13/14 equal, MSFT 13/14 up); (4) nvda-01 3->miss
  299: FAILS (1) passes 34/42; (2) passes 22/30; (3) passes (AAPL 13/14, MSFT 12/14, NVDA 9/14); (4) msft-04 4->miss, nvda-01 3->miss
Outcome: no row qualifies. Reranking is not recommended for set v2 with this model, windowed or not. Defaults unchanged: reranking-enabled false, cross-encoder.enabled
false, rerank-candidates 20, passage-scoring max-window, window-overlap-tokens 64, max-windows 4. Floors not re-derived (no row qualified).
Against the head rows: windowing repaired the figure slice (12/12 in every windowed row, against 10/12, 9/12, 9/12), removed nvda-11, nvda-14 and msft-12 from the
criterion-4 failures, cut the NVDA top-5 loss by two thirds (one question, 8/14, against three, 6/14; none at overlap 224), and at 40 candidates or overlap 224 raised
aggregate hit@5 above the reference (34/42) with a higher hit@3 (0.785714 against 0.714286); it left nvda-01 outside the top 5 in every row and msft-04 in every row
but 298 (both kind FIGURE, nonFigure slice), and
lowered hit@1 (23/42 to 21, 21, 22, 20). Every windowed row has 2.1 to 2.5 times the head row's median scoring time (windows per call 21, 43, 83.5, 51 against 10, 20, 40, 20 rows).

