Each loss or gain on a question named in the plan's Why section, against the truncation probe (truncation-probe-512.txt: chunk tokens, head-kept tokens W, the
expected phrase's token offset, whether the head cut saw it, the head logit, and the logit of the chunk's text from 200 characters before the phrase,
CrossEncoderTruncationProbe.java.txt line 53, which puts the phrase some tens of tokens into that window: 39 for msft-04, 54 for nvda-11, 59 for nvda-01, counted
with the real tokenizer during the documentation correction; not a production window) and the window
positions windowed scoring actually used (CrossEncoderPairAssembler.windowStarts: starts at 0, advance by W - overlap while a window does not reach the last token,
final window at length - W; W = 509 - question tokens for these questions). The Milestone 1 position sweep (live-test-windows.log, positionSweep) logged the same
answering sentence at +10.29 at a window's start, +5.91 at token 141, +2.56 at 164, -11.09 at 213, -7.10 at 257, +2.57 at 340, +3.45 at 419, +3.06 at 484 (max-window).
  nvda-11 (FIGURE, figure slice; chunk 805, 854 tokens, W 477, answer at 596: not seen by the head cut; head 2.62, answer window 5.26). Head rows 7, 10, 10; windowed
    rows 5, 5, 5, 5 (reference 1). Recovered into the top 5, not to the top. Overlap 64 gives windows at 0 and 377 (854 - 477), so the answer sits 219 tokens into the
    second window, the sweep's trough (-11.09 at 213); overlap 224 gives 0, 253, 377, the answer 343 into the second window (+2.57 at 340 in the sweep) and 219 into the
    third, and the rank is still 5, behind chunks 852, 881, 873 and 851 (diagnostic order at the defaults, diagnostic-defaults.txt). Consistent with position
    sensitivity; the sweep is synthetic filler and the logits of chunk 805's windows for this question were not measured.
  nvda-14 (FIGURE, figure slice; chunk 872, 996 tokens, W 477, answer at 820: not seen; head -0.26, answer window 4.78). Head rows 7, miss, miss; windowed rows
    1, 1, 1, 2 (reference 1). Fully recovered: overlap 64 windows at 0, 413, 519 put the answer 407 into the second window and 301 into the third; overlap 224
    (0, 253, 506, 519) 314 into the third and 301 into the fourth, rank 2 behind chunk 873.
  msft-12 (FIGURE, figure slice; chunk 519, 605 tokens, W 490, answer at 544: not seen; head -1.84, answer window 5.14). Head rows 5, 6, 6; windowed rows 2 in all
    four (reference 2). Recovered. The chunk is 115 tokens longer than W, so both overlaps give the same windows (0 and 115) and the answer sits 429 into the second.
  nvda-01 (FIGURE, nonFigure slice; chunk 805, 854 tokens, W 489, answer at 485: the head cut kept only its first four tokens; head -1.75, answer window 5.03; in
    the probe's head ranking of all 162 NVDA chunks 805 was 30th, with 852 at 5.75 and 873 at 5.62). Head rows 9, miss, miss; windowed rows 8, miss, miss, miss
    (reference 3). Not recovered, and not a truncation loss: overlap 64 windows at 0 and 365 put the answer about 120 tokens into the second window, inside a scored
    window. The probe's 5.03 did not measure that window: it scored the text from 200 characters before the phrase, the phrase 59 tokens in, and the sweep changes
    between those depths (+9.42 at 54, +8.09 at 98, +5.91 at 141), so 5.03 does not bound the production window's logit, which was not measured. Chunk 805 is the
    third fused candidate, so every row scores it; it ranks 8 at 10 candidates and outside the reranked top 10 at 20 and 40. The reranked order at the defaults is
    852, 873, 864, 851, 842, 881, 872, 857, 800, 863 (diagnostic-defaults.txt), so the answering table row scores below those chunks in its best window: inferred
    from the ranks, not measured. Overlap 224 (windows 0, 265, 365; the answer 220 and 120 tokens in) leaves it a miss too. One of the two
    questions that fail criterion 4 in every windowed row but 298 (298: nvda-01 alone).
  msft-04 (FIGURE, nonFigure slice; chunk 466, 693 tokens, W 480, answer at 606: not seen; head -10.68, answer window 0.20; the probe's head ranking of all 263
    MSFT chunks put 467 first at 3.04 and 466 150th). Head rows 10, miss, 1 (chunk 467); windowed rows 8, miss, 1 (chunk 467), miss (reference 4, chunk 466).
    The chunk is 213 tokens longer than W and both strides (416, 256) overshoot its end, so both overlaps give the same windows (0 and 213), the answer 393 tokens into
    the second, whose logit was not measured (the probe's text from 200 characters before the phrase, 39 tokens in, scored 0.20, below chunk 467's 3.04). Chunk 467
    (1,564 characters; 391 is the stored characters / 4 token_count, 282 WordPiece tokens with the real tokenizer, so one window at W 480; the following chunk of the
    same section, holding the same sentence from character 96 in the database) is not among the first 20 fused candidates (inferred from the ranks: first of 40 in
    298, it would rank first in any row whose candidates included it) and enters only at 40 candidates, where the reranker puts it first (rows 250 and 298):
    truncation plus the short-chunk edge the plan names. At 20 candidates the reranked order at the defaults is 514, 516, 573, 637, 635, 642, 518, 645, 512, 641
    (diagnostic-defaults.txt), chunks 466 and 467 absent; at 10 candidates (296) chunk 466 ranks 8. The other question failing criterion 4 in rows 296, 297 and 299.
  msft-10 (chunk 637, 737 tokens, W 495, answer at 620: not seen; head -9.52, answer window 9.88): rank 1 in every row; the head rows matched the alternative chunk
    635, the windowed rows match 637 itself (the answer 378 tokens into the second window). A gain in the matched chunk, not in rank.
  msft-13 (chunk 523, 734 tokens, W 483, answer at 630: not seen; head -1.66, answer window 7.73): rank 1 in every row through the alternative chunk 524 under every
    rerank row, head and windowed. No change.
  aapl-05 (chunk 190, 808 tokens, W 500, answer at 655: not seen; head -6.63, answer window 5.06): rank 1 (chunk 190) in the reference, 2 (the alternative chunk 246)
    in every rerank row, head and windowed alike. Windowing (answer 347 tokens into the second window at overlap 64; 379 and 347 at overlap 224) did not lift chunk 190
    above 246. Still in the top 5.
  nvda-02, nvda-04: no match in every row, as before (the answering chunks are not among the reranker's candidates; see the 2026-09-13 nvda-02 retrieval check).
  nvda-09: no match in eight rows, rank 2 (chunk 879) in 299 only. Chunk 879 is not in the probe (no match in 247 and 250), so its token positions were not measured;
    the phrase begins at character 3,150 of its 3,827, in the last quarter of the chunk. It is among the first 20 fused candidates (299 reranked it to 2 from 20
    candidates) and stays a miss at 20 and 40 candidates under overlap 64 (297, 298) and under head (249, 250), so the 224 overlap's extra window, whose start is
    nearer the phrase, is what lifted it: consistent with position sensitivity, one question, not probed with the tokenizer.
  nvda-07: no match -> 8, 9, 8 (chunk 770) at 20 candidates and above (head 6, 7); still outside the top 5. msft-08: no match -> 2 (chunk 547) at 20 and 40 candidates,
    as under head; still no match at 10. nvda-05: 10 -> no match at 20 candidates and above, as under head.
