What enabling would take (recorded, not done; Amendment 2: no default flip, the model files are gitignored). No row qualifies, so there is no recommendation. The row
nearest the rule is 299: it passes criteria 1 to 3 and fails 4 on msft-04 and nvda-01 alone; its properties would be rag.retrieval.cross-encoder.enabled=true
(RAG_CROSS_ENCODER_ENABLED=true), rag.retrieval.reranking-enabled=true, rag.retrieval.cross-encoder.window-overlap-tokens=224, rerank-candidates 20 (default), and it
would cost 1.3 s per retrieval at 20 candidates (max 1,612 ms, under the 2,000 ms timeout by about 0.4 s, measured on sequential calls from one evaluation client
only; the rerank executor runs two scoring calls at once and the recommendation flow runs specialists in parallel, so the margin under concurrent retrievals is
unmeasured). Its top-5 changes against 295: msft-01, msft-07, msft-08, nvda-09 in; msft-04, msft-05, nvda-01 out. The best-MRR row 298 (40 candidates) needs
rerank-timeout-ms 4000 (27 of 42 evaluation calls and the warm-up call over 2,000 ms) and 2.1 s per retrieval, and fails NVDA (8/14) as well as criterion 4 (nvda-01).

