Corrections, 2026-09-13, after Milestone 2 Scrutiny (documentation only; no new run, snapshot, or evaluation; each figure rechecked with a script against the
snapshots, latency-298.txt, the truncation probe and its source, the database, and token counts from the real tokenizer and models/ tokenizer.json):
  - Run 4 and What enabling would take: 27 of the 42 evaluation calls were over 2,000 ms, not 28; the 28th such call was the topK=5 warm-up (2,403 ms).
    The 3aeaa87 commit message also says 28.
  - Other movements: 13 other questions, not 14 (29 questions are named above; the 25 whose rank or chunk changes are among them).
  - Against the head rows: the NVDA loss falls by two thirds (three questions to one), it does not halve; nvda-01 is out of the top 5 in 298 as well.
  - nvda-01: the probe's 5.03 scored the text from 200 characters before the phrase (the phrase 59 tokens in), not the production second window (about 120
    tokens in); the loss within the best window is inferred from the ranks. Same wording fix for msft-05's 2.90 and msft-04's 0.20.
  - msft-04: chunk 467 is 282 WordPiece tokens (391 is the stored characters / 4 estimate); the sentence starts at character 96, not 123; at 10 candidates
    chunk 466 ranks 8 (296), so "absent at 10 and 20 candidates" was wrong.
  - The probe description: the rescored text starts 200 characters before the phrase, not "about 50 tokens ahead" in general.
